cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use webMARS in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "webMARS: a browser implementation of the MARS MIPS 4.5 assembler and simulator"
abstract: >-
  webMARS is a single-page browser implementation of the MARS MIPS 4.5 assembler
  and simulator. It provides an editor, a MIPS32 assembler, an instruction-level
  functional runtime, the classic MARS tool set, and the Pipeline Lab, an
  explicitly separate and versioned five-stage cycle-accurate teaching model.
  Compatibility claims are published as a generated matrix with per-capability
  evidence in docs/comparison-matrix.md.
type: software
version: "0.6.3"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/codigoavulso/webMARS"
url: "https://webmars.nfiles.top/"
keywords:
  - MIPS
  - MARS
  - computer architecture
  - assembler
  - simulator
  - pipeline
  - computer science education
authors:
  # Recorded as the repository identity. Replace with legal names before
  # minting a DOI for an archived release.
  - name: "codigoavulso"
    alias: "codigoavulso"
references:
  - type: software
    title: "MARS: MIPS Assembler and Runtime Simulator, version 4.5"
    notes: >-
      webMARS targets practical compatibility with MARS 4.5. Differences are
      documented in docs/comparison-matrix.md.
    authors:
      - family-names: Vollmar
        given-names: Kenneth
      - family-names: Sanderson
        given-names: Pete
